-- title:
--   Stalks of the mod p fibre of the X₁(Mp) model have dimension ≤ 1
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field $\mathbb{Q}(X_1(Mp)) =$ [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$, and let $K$ carry an $A$-algebra structure compatible with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be a nonzero element whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the base change of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1} \cdot \mathrm{jNumQ}(q)$ of the modular invariant. Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$ with an $A$-algebra structure. Form the fibre product of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L258), the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ of the two-chart model obtained by gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebras `chartAlgFin A K j` and `chartAlgInf A K j` of $K$ along the middle chart, with $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$. Then for every point $z$ of this fibre product, the Krull dimension of the local ring of the fibre product at $z$ is at most $1$.
--
--   The assertion is that every local ring of the characteristic $p$ fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the ring of integers at $p$ of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$, base-changed to an arbitrary field of characteristic $p$, has dimension at most one; it rests on the module-finiteness of the chart algebras over $A[j]$ and the invariance of dimension under integral extensions. It feeds the study of the special fibre of this model: the descent of regularity in the arithmetic genus count, the identification of irreducible components of the fibre over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, and the dimension bound for stalks above the closed point.
